{title: Search Me and Know Me}
{subtitle: Psalm 139}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 69}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm7] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]LORD, you have searched me and you know [F/A]me
[Gm7]You know when I sit down and when I rise
[Eb]You [Bb]discern my thoughts from far away
You are familiar with all [Gm7]my ways
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Search me, O God, and [Eb]know my [Bb]heart
Test me and know my anxious [F]thoughts
See if there is any offen[Gm7]sive way in me
And lead me in the way ev[Eb]erlasting
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I tried to run where the dark is deep
Where the sea runs out and the shadows sleep
I rode [F/A]the [Gm7]wings of the early dawn
But your hand was [Eb]there [Bb]as I travelled on
Even the darkness [F/A]is not dark to [Gm7]you
The night shines like the day
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Search me, O God, and know [Cm7]my heart
Test me and [F]know my anxious thoughts
[Gm7]See if [F/A]there is any of[Bb]fensive way in me
And lead me [F]in the way everlasting
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Before [Gm]my mother knew my face
You knit me in [Eb]a hidden place
You wove my frame where no eye could look
And [Gm]wrote my days into your book
I praise [Eb]you, for I am awesomely and wonder[Bb]fully made
Your works are wonderful; my [F]soul knows it well
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
How precious to [Gm]me are your thoughts, O [Eb]God!
How vast is their num[Bb]ber!
If I could count them, they would [Eb]outnumber the grains of sand
When I awake, [Bb]I am still with you
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Search me, O [F]God, and know my heart
Test me and know [Gm]my anxious thoughts
See if there is any [Eb]offensive way in me
And lead me in the way everlasting
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Lead me in the way everlasting
{end_of_verse}

